# A record carried round a loop, with a string field each pass extends.
#
# `spin` reads `st.body` once, as the first piece of the template that makes
# the next body, and reads `st` nowhere but its fields. Every record that
# reaches `spin` holds a body nothing else holds: the first is built from
# `grown`, which reads its accumulator only into templates and hands back a
# string of its own, and each later one holds the template's result. So the
# join writes into the body it was given, and a pass costs the bytes it adds.
# Until 2026-10-23 each pass copied the whole body into a new string, so
# alloc_bytes grew with the square of the passes.
type state
  count
  body

fn grown 0 acc
  acc

fn grown n acc
  grown (n - 1) "{acc}{acc}"

fn spin 0 st
  st

fn spin n st
  spin (n - 1) (state (st.count + 1) "{st.body}{st.count % 10}")

pub play = print (length (spin 2000 (state 0 (grown 10 "x"))).body)
